            <ArticleTitle>Allele NAT2*5 determines resistance to bronchial asthma in children.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>575-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>NAT2*5 allele was found in 54.8% healthy children and 35.9% children with bronchial asthma, i.e. the risk of bronchial asthma was considerably lower in individuals carrying NAT2*5 allele. NAT2*5 allele manifests itself in both homo- and heterozygous states.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
